                    <div class="bs-callout bs-callout-info" >
                        <h4>Hunter Education</h4>
                        <p>Our Hunter Education classes have been moved and can be viewed online at <a href="https://app.fw.ky.gov/edcourse" target="_blank">Education Course Events</a>.</p>
                    </div>

                    <span id="MainContent_LabelEvents"><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>3-D ACRHERY AT JONES-KEENEY WMA ARCHERY RANGE HOSTED BY CALDWELL  - <span style='color:#333;'>Caldwell County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=69879'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p>30 target 3-D archery course located in the woods and hills of the Jones-Keeney WMA. Hosted by the Caldwell County Sportsman Club. Our targets range from a small armadillo to a buffalo. Your get a unique experience unlike any other, we have moving targets and at times a steel change target. We welcome all ages and skill levels. We use ASA scoring with club rules. We hope to see you sometime out there. We also shoot 3-D year around out side. Also, we are only club that shoot 3-D after 2pm. </p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>1/25/2026</div><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>9/26/2026</div><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>9/27/2026</div><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/24/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Kids Events, Conservation Organizations / Sportsman Clubs, Meetings / Banquets, Other</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>2nd Annual Night 3-D Archery Shoot at Jones Keeney WMA Range Host - <span style='color:#333;'>Caldwell County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=69887'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p>You will be shooting  20 3-D archery targets at night at the Jones-Keeney WMA range through the woods and hills.  Bring your own light and fun</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/10/2026</div><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/11/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Kids Events, Conservation Organizations / Sportsman Clubs, Other</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>Salato—Sensational Snakes  - <span style='color:#333;'>Franklin County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=71261'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p>Discover the different species of snakes in Kentucky and their amazing abilities. This program may use live animals as well as shells, skins, and other props.</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/1/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Salato Wildlife Education Center, Featured KDFWR Events</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>Salato—Toxins Talk - <span style='color:#333;'>Franklin County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=71262'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p>In this educator-led talk learn the key differences between venom and poison, bust myths about these toxins, and discover how wildlife with these fascinating adaptations use their chemical compounds for survival. A great program for those with curious minds!</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/1/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Salato Wildlife Education Center, Featured KDFWR Events</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>Salato--Owl Program  - <span style='color:#333;'>Franklin County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=71263'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p>Let's learn about owls! Join one of our conservation educators to learn about Kentucky’s native owls and their adaptations. This program may feature props and a live animal.</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/2/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Salato Wildlife Education Center, Featured KDFWR Events</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>Salato—Reptiles of Kentucky  - <span style='color:#333;'>Franklin County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=71264'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p>Let’s learn about reptiles! Reptiles include snakes, lizards, and turtles. They share unique traits called adaptations that help them survive in their environments. This program may include live animals as well as shells, skins, and other props.</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/2/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Salato Wildlife Education Center, Featured KDFWR Events</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>Salato--Wild Encounter - <span style='color:#333;'>Franklin County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=71265'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p>Now is your chance to learn about some of the animals that call Salato home! We'll have staff on hand to answer questions and discuss species from our collection of native wildlife.</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/3/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Salato Wildlife Education Center, Featured KDFWR Events</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>Salato--Gnarly Natives: Plants & Critters to Watch Out For - <span style='color:#333;'>Franklin County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=71266'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p>Join a conservation educator for an informative session on how to stay safe outdoors! Learn how to spot poison ivy, identify stinging insects, venomous snakes, and more! You’ll discover how to avoid harm while respecting the important role these species play in our ecosystem.</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/3/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Salato Wildlife Education Center, Featured KDFWR Events</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>NKSSA Thursday Night Trap Shoots - <span style='color:#333;'>Grant County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 t