-body'><p>Metallic Silhouette match sanctioned by the International Handgun Metallic Silhouette Association.  Sponsored by the Northern Kentucky Straight Shooters Association. Weather permitting, over 50 degrees and not raining.</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>5/31/2026</div><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>6/21/2026</div><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>8/30/2026</div><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>9/27/2026</div><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/25/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Conservation Organizations / Sportsman Clubs</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>NRA Basic Instructor Training - <span style='color:#333;'>Grant County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=69980'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p>NRA certified class that is a prerequisite for any instructor training classes. Sponsored by the Northern KY Straight Shooters Association. Pre-registration required.  Registration information is on our website: www.nkssa.org.
</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/3/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Educational / Workshops / Seminars , Conservation Organizations / Sportsman Clubs</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>NRA Basic Rifle Course - <span style='color:#333;'>Grant County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=69982'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p>NRA Approved Rifle course for anyone who would like to know more about how their rifle operates and how to improve their marksmanship.  Sponsored by the Northern Kentucky Straight Shooters Association.  Preregistration required.  Registration information is on our website: www.nkssa.org</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/17/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Educational / Workshops / Seminars , Conservation Organizations / Sportsman Clubs</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>United Trappers of Kentucky Fall Meet - <span style='color:#333;'>Lawrence County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=71182'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p>https://forum.kentuckytrappers.[long].gif</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/2/2026</div><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/3/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Educational / Workshops / Seminars , Outdoor Shows / Exhibitions / Festivals, Hunting Events (not Hunter Education)</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>Deer Processing - Georgetown  - <span style='color:#333;'>Scott County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=71267'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p><p>This course will teach you about how to skin, process, and package a full deer. Whether you are a beginner or an experienced hunter this course can help sharpen skills and add tips and tricks to making the processing of game easier. This course will include a short classroom portion about hunting and deer as a whole before going outside to a covered patio to watch a processing demonstration. Depending on number of participants and how many deer are donated for this course there may be an optional hands on processing experience with the guided help of an instructor.</p>

<p>Learn about:</p>

<p>Safety, food processing, deer biology, hunting, tools, skinning, preserving meat safely, parts of the deer, muscle groups and uses for each, recipes for venison, and more!</p>
</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/10/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Educational / Workshops / Seminars , Featured KDFWR Events, Hunting Events (not Hunter Education), Field To Fork</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>Muzzleloader 101 - Georgetown  - <span style='color:#333;'>Scott County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=71268'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p><p>This course will teach you a brief history of muzzleloaders and how they operate as well as give hands on experience loading and firing several. Whether you are new to muzzleloaders or want some additional practice before muzzleloader season this course has something to offer for everyone. This course will begin with a short classroom portion focused on safety, firearm handling, and muzzleloader parts and their functions. After this we will move to the range on site and practice what was taught in the classroom in a controlled environment.</p>

<p>Learn about:</p>

<p>Range procedures and safety, firearm history, firearms handling, muzzleloading rifle operation and safety, and more!</p>
</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/10/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Educational / Workshops / Seminars , Featured KDFWR Events, Hunting Events (not Hunter Education), Field To Fork</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4> Field to Fork Mentor Squirrel Hunt - Georgetown  - <span style='color:#333;'>Scott County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=71269'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p><p>This course will teach you the basics of hunting squirrels in Kentucky. Whether you are an experienced sportsman or a first-time hunter, this course will teach you the skills and knowledge you need to get started in squirrel hunting. This course will begin with a classroom portion focused on squirrel biology and behavior, hunting regulations, safety, best practices, and processing. After the classroom portion there will be a range portion offered to familiarize new hunters with their firearms and certify anyone who needs their hunter education range day certification. Finally, participants will be paired with a mentor to go on the hunt at the same location as the rest of the course!</p>

<p>You will learn: location selection, shooting techniques, firearm safety, field dressing demo, hunting methods, and more!</p>
</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/16/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Educational / Workshops / Seminars , Featured KDFWR Events, Hunting Events (not Hunter Education), Mentored Hunt, Field To Fork</p></div></div><div class='panel panel-default'><div class='panel-heading'><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8 col-lg-9'><h4>Firearm Ownership and Maintenance  - <span style='color:#333;'>Scott County</span></h4></div><div class='col-md-4 col-lg-3 text-right'><a class='btn btn-primary btn-block' href='Detail.aspx?ID=71270'>View Event&nbsp;<i class='fas fa-arrow-alt-circle-right'></i></a></div></div></div><div class='panel-body'><p><p>This course will teach you about firearm ownership in regardless to legal possession, maintenance/repairs, and storage/transport. This course is for all firearm owners regardless of experience or age. This class will be in a classroom with a short powerpoint covering safety, firearm laws, and proper care of firearms. Afterward there will time to practice with a hands on portion disassembling and cleaning firearms.</p>

<p>Learn about:</p>

<p>firearm safety, laws regarding firearms, firearm storage, firearm transport, firearm cleaning, and more!</p>
</p><p style='margin-bottom:0px;'><strong>Dates:</strong></p><div class='row' style='margin-bottom:15px;'><div class='col-xs-4 col-md-2'>10/28/2026</div></div><p><strong>Categories:</strong><br />Educational / Workshops / Seminars , Featured KDFWR Events, Hunting Events (not Hunter Education), Field To Fork</p></div></div><div class='bs-callout bs-callout-warning'><h4>Didn't find the event you were looking for?</h4><p>Try changing the Month/Year, Location, or the Category.</p></div></span>
